WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:12.799
Huawei says the Mate X is the fastest foldable
5G phone in the world.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:16.610
It appears to be a well-thought-out design,
too.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:22.310
The display folds back to become a 6.6 inch
display, bigger that then screen on the foldable

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.380
phone Samsung unveiled last week
But the Huawei device won't be out till at

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.820
least June.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.450
Those who can wait will need deep pockets,
and not just to fit the phone.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.340
It will cost 2300 euros in Europe.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.829
And in Barcelona, it's look, don't touch.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:44.449
The 5.4-millimeter-thin phone is only on display
behind much thicker Plexiglas.

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:49.819
I still think the Mate X is quite amazing.

00:00:49.819 --> 00:00:59.199
Amazing me because the shape and the design
of the whole foldables.

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:01.410
I think it is very useful.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:06.120
I think it is too expensive for this device.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.469
It is not ready.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:08.710
It has a lot of failures.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.140
I can see right now – the little stuff there.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:17.670
I think for the endproduct when they release
the product it is going to be ready.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:24.299
Royole - another Chinese manufacturer, thinks
of itself as the trendsetter here.

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:31.700
It already sells foldable smartphones - in
Europe they cost just under 1400 euros.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:37.570
With our flexible screen you can make the
screen foldable.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:42.429
So that you can have both the porabilties
and also the large screen viewer experience.

00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:46.200
So it totally changes the way of the traditional
design of smartphones.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.420
Give it more design rooms, innovation of the
smartphone.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.990
But it's Huawei that's the star of the show
today.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:58.840
The company is is going big on 5G - the future
mobile communications standard that will see

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.570
all sorts of home devices connected to super-fast
internet.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.960
For now Huawei is concentrating on flashy
displays.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.160
And while the company's president has rejected
US warnings that the Chinese government could

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:25.470
use its technology to gather intelligence
- here at the show, it prefers to

00:02:25.470 --> 00:04:28.290
dance around 
the issue.

